      {
        "id": 95319,
        "name": "Ed",
        "username": "Ed1",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/958977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-09T12:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chromium_Man\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chromium_Man:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm a big fan of the recently put forth theory that Con is Bunker.&nbsp; (I'm sorry I don't remember who suggested it.)&nbsp; The basis for this theory is that there is a card called \"Con's Bunker\" which could actually mean \"Con is Bunker\".&nbsp; It doesn't get any simpler than that  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><span>In accordance to this hypothesis, check the incap side from Termi-nation Bunker. To me, it shows like Omnitron is checking out a part of the Bunker suit. It could imply something?&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><img alt=\"termbuba.png\" src=\"http://sotm.wdfiles.com/local--files/heroes:bunker/termbuba.png\" width=\"\" height=\"\"></p>\n<p>Edit: I wanted to decrease the size of the picture but failed</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:07.556Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
